","co":"ETERNAL LIMITED","has":true,"layer":"Platform Intermediation & Last-Mile Logistics","q":"Q4FY26","sec":"Digital Commerce / Quick Commerce & Food Delivery Aggregation","st":[{"status":"Sharpest short-term","subtheme":"Quick-commerce, omnichannel & retail expansion","tag":"Consumption","theme":"Consumer & Retail","tier":"1"}],"thesis":"Two things changed this quarter, and both are structural. First, management **raised the Blinkit long-term steady-state margin from the 5–6% range to the 6% top end**, and paired it with a first-ever **GAAP EBIT margin target of 4%** — a shift from \"we'll be profitable\" to a specific, auditable unit-economics contract. Second, they **rewrote the store model**: capex per store **₹1cr → ₹2.5cr (+150%)**, NOV-per-store-per-day up only 60%, and net working capital guided down **18 → 14 → 12 days** — explicitly framing the whole thing as *\"we are open with these numbers moving around... as long as the math on ROCE is stacking up well.\"* Meanwhile Q1 was called the **peak of competitive intensity to date**, and management's core claim is that discount-led rivals are in a trap they cannot exit. Blinkit grew **+21% QoQ in volume** with MTUs **>30mn**, on *fewer* store adds and *lower* marketing spend — the strongest evidence yet that the growth is not being bought.","trig":[]},"lm":"","m":315711,"mem":0,"pdd":"","prev_stage":3,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"r":null,"s":"ETERNAL","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"292.0","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"11.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"0.9","vpe_zone_cumul_df":"0.6"},"t":""}},"s":"ETERNAL"}